Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: bfd/cofflink.c
Line: 1232
Function: dores_com
Bug type: out-of-bounds-read
CWE: CWE-125
Explanation: Uses strtoul(ptr, &ptr, 0) on a pointer into the .drectve section data that is not guaranteed to be NUL-terminated. strtoul reads until a non-digit or NUL, so if the numeric field extends to the end of the section, it can read past the allocated buffer. This is reachable from process_embedded_commands() via the -heap/-stack directives.

